  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2020-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(a = \\log_2 3,\\) so \\(\\log_3 2 = \\tfrac1a.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\log_2 6 + \\log_3 6 \\\\ {}= (1 + \\log_2 3) \\\\ \\quad {}+ (1 + \\log_3 2) \\\\ {}= 2 + a + \\frac1a. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nMeanwhile \\(\\left(\\sqrt{\\log_2 3} + \\sqrt{\\log_3 2}\\right)^2\\) \\(= a + \\frac1a + 2\\sqrt{a \\cdot \\tfrac1a}\\) \\(= a + \\frac1a + 2,\\) which equals the expression above.\n\nTaking square roots, \\(\\sqrt{\\log_2 6 + \\log_3 6}\\) \\(= \\sqrt{\\log_2 3} + \\sqrt{\\log_3 2}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(\\log_2 6 = 1 + \\log_2 3\\) and \\(\\log_3 6 = 1 + \\log_3 2\\)",
        "Compare with \\(\\left(\\sqrt{\\log_2 3} + \\sqrt{\\log_3 2}\\right)^2,\\) using \\(\\log_2 3 \\cdot \\log_3 2 = 1\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
